ami2ha @VERSION@ -- a Home Assistant client for AmigaOS
=======================================================

Read your sensors and flip your switches from a real Amiga.


Installing
----------

Double-click the Install icon.

From a Shell you have to name the Installer in full, because it is
not on the command path:

    SYS:System/Installer Install

(On AmigaOS 3.1 and earlier it lives in SYS:Utilities instead.)

Or skip the installer entirely -- it is one program:

    MakeDir Work:ami2ha
    Copy ami2ha.020 Work:ami2ha/ami2ha      ; ami2ha.000 on a 68000/68010
    Copy ami2ha.guide Work:ami2ha
    Copy icons/ami2ha.info Work:ami2ha      ; optional, for the icon

Then see "Getting it running" below.


What you need
-------------

    AmigaOS 3.0 or newer
    a TCP/IP stack offering bsdsocket.library
        -- Roadshow, AmiTCP, Miami, or UAE's own emulation
    MUI 3.8 or newer, for the dashboard
        -- the command line modes work without it
    AmiSSL 5, only if you connect over https
        -- opened on demand, so plain http needs nothing

A 68020 is comfortable. The 68000 build works but is slow.


Before it can connect
---------------------

You need a long-lived access token from Home Assistant. In a
browser: click your user name at the bottom left, open the
Security tab, and create one under "Long-lived access tokens".
It is shown once, so copy it there and then.

Put it in a file of its own, ha.token, in the installation drawer.

That token can control everything in your house. Keep the file to
yourself, and do not pass the token on a command line where your
shell history would keep it.


Getting it running
------------------

Put your token in a file, then let ami2ha write its own
configuration by asking your server what to show:

    Work:ami2ha/ami2ha 192.168.1.100 TOKENFILE=Work:ami2ha/ha.token
             LABEL=amiga WRITECONFIG=Work:ami2ha/ami2ha.cfg

From then on that one file holds everything, and starting it is:

    Work:ami2ha/ami2ha CONFIG=Work:ami2ha/ami2ha.cfg GUI

To start it from Workbench instead, write the setting into the icon
once:

    Work:ami2ha/ami2ha CONFIG=Work:ami2ha/ami2ha.cfg WRITEICON

If your server is behind https, add TLS -- the port then defaults to
443 instead of 8123:

    Work:ami2ha/ami2ha myhouse.example.com TLS TOKENFILE=Work:ami2ha/ha.token

The certificate is checked by default. A self-signed one needs NOVERIFY
as well, which keeps the traffic encrypted but stops proving who is
answering, so use it only on a network you trust. The manual has more.

Only CONFIG belongs in the icon's tool types. The address, the token
file, the label and the whole layout live in the configuration file.


The manual
----------

ami2ha.guide covers the rest: choosing which entities appear,
the dashboard, the settings window, starting it from Workbench,
the ARexx port, and what to do when something does not work.

Open it with MultiView, or double-click it.


